          %h2#cartan_geometry Cartan geometry
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"}> Smooth manifolds
            , such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetimes"} spacetimes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
            and its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_1.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^d
            (see also at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+coordinate+systems"} geometry of physics – coordinate systems
          %p
            It is clear that here it is crucial that
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            is regarded with its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+structure"} smooth structure
          %p
            But
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^d
            also has (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+group"}> smooth
            )
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            structure. As such it is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/translation+group"} translation group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Newtonian+mechanics"} Newtonian mechanics
            this group structure plays a key role, as it allows for instance to say what in means that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particle"} particle
            propagates along a straight
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trajectory"} trajectory
          %p
            With the dawn of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+relativity"} general relativity
            and its “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+covariance"}> general covariance
            ” it was finally understood that this is a bit too naive:
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field"} free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particles"} particles
            propagate on straight lines in
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            only
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimally
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/force"} force
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
          %p
            This has a straightforward visualization in 2-dimensions: visualize a bumpy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedded
            in
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3
            (for instance a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sphere"} 2-sphere
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
            and visualize the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent"} tangent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane"} plane
            to that point, which is an
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curve"} curve
            in
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            that emanates from
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            such that the point where it touches
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            follows the curve.
          %p
            Under this map from curves in the plane to curves in the
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
            now map to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geodesics"} geodesics
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            follow.
          %p
            The most popular way to formalize this is the modern concept of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Levi-Civita+connection"} Levi-Civita connection
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            on
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (which in the above example is induced from the canonical one on the embedding space
            = succeed ")." do
              %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3
          %p
            But
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%89lie+Cartan"} Élie Cartan
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+connections"} affine connections
            much closer resembles this picture of a “local model space with group structure” doing “rolling without slipping” over
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+connection"} Cartan connection
          %p
            Here one regards the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+group"} Euclidean group
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_19.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Iso(n)
            of all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometries"} isometries
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_20.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rotation+group"} rotation group
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_21.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Iso
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(d) \hookrightarrow Iso(d)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+group"} quotient group
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_22.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{R}^d \simeq Iso(d)/SO(d)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The structure of “rolling without sliding” is then formalized in the concept of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+connection"} Cartan connection
            by saying
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %strong rolling
                – there is an
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_23.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Iso
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Iso(d)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
                on
                %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_24.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                (the group
                = succeed "," do
                  %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_25.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Iso
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Iso(d)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
                on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_26.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^d
            %li
              %p
                %strong without sliding
                – such that there is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+of+the+structure+group"} reduction of the structure group
                to
                %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_27.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SO
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(d)
                (this makes the original
                = succeed "-bundle" do
                  %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_28.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Iso
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Iso(n)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated
                to it the actual
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_29.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^d
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
          %p
            and such that under this reduction the connection at each point infinitesimally identifies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+space"} tangent space
            of
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_30.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with the abstract copy of
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_31.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi d
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Iso
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^d \simeq Iso(d)/SO(d)
          %p
            This has an evident generalization where we consider any inclusion
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_32.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
