                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{L}_{WZW}
                  \\;\colon\;
                  \\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1 \vert N}
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathbf{B}^{p+1} (\mathbb{R}/\Gamma)_{conn}
          %p
            But for the moment it is helpful for simplicity to stay at the rational/infinitesimal/
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_104.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            \-algebraic level. All what we find here lifts as expected under
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
          %p
            So, now according to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} local prequantum
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+condition"} boundary condition
            for this Lagrangian is a diagram of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_105.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
