                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\widehat{\mathbb{R}}}^{d-1,1 \vert N}
              are precisely the dg-algebras used at least since (
              %a{:href => "#DAuriaFre82"}> D’Auria-Fré 82
              ) in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fr%C3%A9+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fré formulation of supergravity
          %p
            This is shown in (
            %a{:href => "#FSS13"}> FSS 13
            ) using a characterization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullbacks"} homotopy pullbacks
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+L-infinity+algebras"} model structure for L-infinity algebras
            derived in (
            %a{:href => "#FRS13b"}> FRS 13b
            ).
          %p
            But now from this we see that on
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_117.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
