          %h2#TheCompletedBrainScan The completed brane scan
          %p
            This gives a curious direct identification between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra+cohomology"} L-∞ algebra cohomology
            and brane intersection laws: every
            = succeed "-extension" do
              %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_123.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            = succeed "-cocycle" do
              %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_124.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+WZW+sigma-model"} higher WZW sigma-model
            for some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane"} super p-brane
            wich may end on a super-
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_125.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde p
            \-brane. It turns out that this reasoning reproduces the
            %em completed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring+theory"} superstring theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            together with the information that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+string"} fundamental string
            may end on them, as well as the sigma-model for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            with its tensor multiplet fields (
            %a{:href => "#FSS13"}> FSS 13
            ) and the information that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            may end on it. These maps out much of the key statements about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            (and does so in a precise/rigorous way).
