          %p
            %strong Proposition
          %p
            We may construct the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+n-bundle"} prequantum (p+1)-bundle
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_127.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mi WZW
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ^
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                        %mi WZW
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Γ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{L}_{WZW}
                  \\;\colon\;
                  {\widehat \mathbb{R}}^{d-1,1\vert N}
                  \\stackrel{\mathbf{L}_{WZW}}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\mathbf{B}^{p+1} (\mathbb{R}/\Gamma)_{conn}
          %p
            for all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane"} super p-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-models"} sigma-models
            via a kind of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#FSS13"} FSS13
          %h2#anomalyfree_higher_sigmamodels_via_higher_stringlifts_of_cartan_connections Anomaly-free higher sigma-models via higher string-lifts of Cartan connections
          %p
            All would be done and said if
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            were fixed to be a give
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super+Minkowski+spacetime"} extended super Minkowski spacetime
          %p
            But of course the key now is that in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            instead spacetime
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_128.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            only locally looks this way, and globally is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+connection"} Cartan connection
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+group"} super Poincaré group
            or its higher analogs acting on an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super+Minkowski+spacetime"} extended super Minkowski spacetime
          %p
            What we need to solve the gluing problem for the higher WZW term and hence cancel its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+anomaly"} classical anomaly
            is that on
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_129.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            itself there is a WZW term
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_130.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mi WZW
                    %mi global
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Γ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{L}_{WZW}^{global} \colon X \longrightarrow \mathbf{B}^{p+1}(\mathbb{R}/\Gamma)_{conn}
          %p
            such that for a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
            by local model space as given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+connection"} Cartan connection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+gauge+field"} background gauge field
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %code.maruku-mathml
              \\array{
              {\widehat{\mathbb{R}}}^{d-1,1\vert N}
              \\\
              \\downarrow &amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{\stackrel{\mathbf{L}_{WZW}}}
              \\\
              X
              \&amp;
              \\stackrel{\mathbf{L}_{WZW}^{global}}{\longrightarrow}
              \&amp;
              \\mathbf{B}^{p+1} (\mathbb{R}/\Gamma)_{conn}
              }
              \\,.
          %blockquote
            %p
              I claim that the solution to this globalization problem works as follows, though I have not written this down in full detail yet. Notice that while I write super-Minkowski spacetimes here just for the heck of it, this may be considered much more generally in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Cartan+geometry"} higher Cartan geometry
          %p
            Consider the restriction of the WZW term to any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+disk"} formal disk
            (this is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+geometry"} synthetically
            the
            = succeed "-algebra," do
              %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_131.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    {\widehat{\mathbb{R}}}^{d-1,1\vert N}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{\stackrel{\mathbf{L}_{WZW}}}L_\infty
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+differentiation"} Lie differentiation
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_132.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mi WZW
                    %mi formal
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mo ^
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ^
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
