                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}(p Brane(d\vert N))
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\widehat {\tau}_X}}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  X &amp;\stackrel{\tau_X}{\longrightarrow} &amp; \mathbf{B}GL(d,N)
                  }
          %p
            of the map that classifies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+bundle"} frame bundle
            as discussed at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
            in the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "differential+cohesion#GLnTangentBundles"} Differential cohesion – Frame bundles
          %p
            By the above picture of
            %math#mathml_a0136b00a59018dc879e6912a866dd696f262538_140.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mi Brane
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p Brane(d\vert N)
            it should be plausbile that this is precisely the data needed to carry the WZW turn around with Cartan’s “rolling without slipping”.
